WEBVTT

1
00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:26.916
- It's a round hoopy thing.
- Come on.

2
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.208
What did you steal?

3
00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:30.500
- I got a sugar cube.
- I got a biscuit crumb.

4
00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:33.541
- I got a toenail.
- Oops.

5
00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:34.458
- Dad?
- Yes?

6
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:37.291
On the next sneak,
can we break into the house with the...

7
00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:38.500
What... What's that?

8
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:39.583
- Huh?
- Hm?

9
00:01:40.041 --> 00:01:41.041
Oh, it's a...

10
00:01:42.875 --> 00:01:44.375
Inside! Now!

11
00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.541
It's a... It's...

12
00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:00.541
Funny-looking. Can we eat it?

13
00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:01.875
No! It's a...

14
00:02:01.958 --> 00:02:04.875
Well, it's a robin, I think.

15
00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.833
Hi, Robin.

16
00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.083
Can we keep her?

17
00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:11.375
Well, maybe.

18
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:15.000
After all, she's only one little...

19
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:18.833
...Robin.

20
00:02:20.375 --> 00:02:22.916
- Wow...
- Ow! Ooh! Ow! Ooh!

21
00:02:42.041 --> 00:02:43.041
Wait.

22
00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:45.666
Wait for it.

23
00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:49.666
Okay, let's go slowly...

24
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.000
- Yes! Yes, yes!
- Hey!

25
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:53.291
Ow...

26
00:02:54.958 --> 00:02:58.791
<i>♪ We're on our way to break into a house ♪</i>

27
00:02:58.875 --> 00:03:02.666
<i>♪ Might be a bird
But I sneak just like a mouse ♪</i>

28
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.375
<i>♪ Da-da-da-da ♪</i>

29
00:03:08.458 --> 00:03:11.750
<i>♪ Da-la-la-da-da-da-da! ♪</i>

30
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.500
- So, what are you getting tonight?
- I might get a pie crumb?

31
00:03:18.583 --> 00:03:21.833
- Something moldy, I think.
- Well, I'm going to sneak a whole crust.

32
00:03:22.458 --> 00:03:25.833
Well, I'm going to sneak
a whole sandwich.

33
00:03:25.916 --> 00:03:26.791
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

34
00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:29.750
- You can't sneak a whole sandwich.
- How do you sneak a sandwich?

35
00:03:30.416 --> 00:03:32.166
- Um...
- Hm.

36
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.166
Like this.

37
00:03:36.166 --> 00:03:37.708
Race you to the fence!

38
00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:41.750
That's in my eye!
Don't do that.

39
00:03:42.958 --> 00:03:44.416
- Pip, you're up front.
- Yes, Dad.

40
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.041
- Dink, don't drag your tail.
- Okay.

41
00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.000
- Flynn, Flin, no showing off.
- All right.

42
00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:48.916
And, Robin...

43
00:03:50.458 --> 00:03:51.500
Got it, Dad!

44
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.875
I didn't say anything.

45
00:03:53.958 --> 00:03:54.791
Robin!

46
00:03:54.875 --> 00:03:56.791
Ro... Robin?

47
00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:10.791
<i>♪ The rules of The Sneak are simple
And thus ♪</i>

48
00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:12.875
<i>♪ Follow them close
You could steal a crust ♪</i>

49
00:04:12.958 --> 00:04:15.000
<i>- ♪ Or a crumpet rind ♪
- ♪ Or a pinch of pie ♪</i>

50
00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:17.750
<i>♪ Or the grease from the tip
Of a soggy french fry ♪</i>

51
00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:20.333
<i>♪ Crumbs and crusts and stale bread ♪</i>

52
00:04:20.416 --> 00:04:22.458
<i>♪ Soggy flakes and bin dregs ♪</i>

53
00:04:22.541 --> 00:04:24.500
<i>♪ Any old leftovers ♪</i>

54
00:04:24.583 --> 00:04:27.208
<i>♪ We'll sneak home with us ♪</i>

55
00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:31.583
<i>♪ First find a secret entrance
Keep your eyes open wide ♪</i>

56
00:04:31.666 --> 00:04:34.083
<i>- ♪ For a hole ♪
- ♪ Or a crack or a window with a gap ♪</i>

57
00:04:34.166 --> 00:04:36.250
<i>♪ Just enough to squeeze inside ♪</i>

58
00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:42.541
<i>♪ Once we're in, we creep around
Tiptoe past without a sound ♪</i>

59
00:04:42.625 --> 00:04:44.750
<i>♪ Keep to the shadows
Don't get heard ♪</i>

60
00:04:44.833 --> 00:04:47.166
<i>♪ Whisper every single word ♪</i>

61
00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.416
<i>♪ Da-di-la-di-da! ♪</i>

62
00:04:49.416 --> 00:04:50.958
- What?
- Come on.

63
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:56.416
<i>♪ Last, the most important
Remember in the who-man place ♪</i>

64
00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.750
<i>♪ They're choosy who's invited ♪</i>

65
00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:03.291
<i>♪ So we must never leave a trace ♪</i>

66
00:05:03.375 --> 00:05:07.416
<i>♪ Crumbs and crusts and stale bread
Soggy flakes and bin dregs ♪</i>

67
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:11.833
<i>♪ Any old leftovers
We'll sneak home with us ♪</i>

68
00:05:12.625 --> 00:05:15.875
A whole sandwich!

69
00:05:16.958 --> 00:05:21.250
<i>♪ When we're done, we disappear
Nobody knows that we were here ♪</i>

70
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.458
<i>- ♪ With crumbs in our hands ♪
- ♪ Warmth in our hearts ♪</i>

71
00:05:24.541 --> 00:05:26.833
<i>♪ And the sludge from the tin
Of a moldy jam tart ♪</i>

72
00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:30.750
<i>- ♪ Don't make a sound ♪</i>
- Robin!

73
00:05:30.833 --> 00:05:33.708
<i>♪ Don't leave a trace
Keep to the shadows, take what we need ♪</i>

74
00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:40.166
<i>♪ The rules of The Sneak are these</i> ♪

75
00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.041
<i>♪ Da-da-doo-da-loo, whoop! ♪</i>

76
00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:47.250
Who-mans!

77
00:06:03.708 --> 00:06:04.583
Robin!

78
00:06:09.208 --> 00:06:12.291
Well, let's not go back there again.

79
00:06:12.375 --> 00:06:15.708
They'll be setting out traps or,

80
00:06:15.791 --> 00:06:17.666
maybe even getting a...

81
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.583
- ...kitten.
- Kittens!

82
00:06:20.166 --> 00:06:22.583
Don't listen to them.

83
00:06:22.666 --> 00:06:25.375
- Nice one, Robin.
- What?

84
00:06:25.458 --> 00:06:28.166
Well, the spoon, and the sandwich, and...

85
00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.708
Pip, enough of that.

86
00:06:29.791 --> 00:06:31.875
Come on. We've still got plenty to eat.

87
00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.625
There's the bag of Earl Grey.

88
00:06:34.916 --> 00:06:37.291
I'm sick of Earl Grey!

89
00:06:40.916 --> 00:06:45.125
All right.
Well, come on now. Off to bed.

90
00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:49.416
It's okay, Robin.
We'll figure this out together.

91
00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:52.583
Yeah. I mean, next time, I'll just...

92
00:06:53.291 --> 00:06:57.125
stay away from... spoons. Yeah.

93
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.500
All that mold!

94
00:07:16.416 --> 00:07:18.791
S-s-sandwich. Mm...

95
00:07:34.958 --> 00:07:37.875
"Oh! Hi, Robin. What's all this?"

96
00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:40.250
"Crumbs? For the whole family?"

97
00:07:41.291 --> 00:07:44.666
"Yeah. It was easy.
Just got them from a who-man house."

98
00:07:45.375 --> 00:07:50.083
"Oh, wow, Robin!
You're the most amazing sneak ever!"

99
00:07:52.375 --> 00:07:53.458
Huh? Hm.

100
00:07:54.375 --> 00:07:56.208
Can't wait to see the look on Pip's face

101
00:07:56.291 --> 00:07:59.125
when I come back
with a crumb the size of his head.

102
00:08:04.708 --> 00:08:05.708
Hm.

103
00:08:06.333 --> 00:08:10.041
No. No. No. No.

104
00:08:10.125 --> 00:08:11.708
Oh, uh, excuse me.

105
00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:14.375
- Do you know where the...
- No! No. No...

106
00:08:14.875 --> 00:08:17.458
Oh. Okay. Thanks anyway.

107
00:08:20.916 --> 00:08:22.500
The who-man house.

108
00:08:25.416 --> 00:08:27.333
<i>♪ Da-dum-dum-dum ♪</i>

109
00:08:27.416 --> 00:08:29.166
<i>♪ Doodloo-doodloo, ba-dum-bum ♪</i>

110
00:08:30.166 --> 00:08:33.708
<i>♪ Doodloo-doodloo, da-dum-dum
Dum-bum-bum-bum ♪</i>

111
00:08:33.791 --> 00:08:35.166
<i>♪ Da-dum-bum-ba ♪</i>

112
00:08:41.875 --> 00:08:44.500
Oh, I'm sorry.
I didn't realize this was a...

113
00:08:47.208 --> 00:08:48.458
...cat house!

114
00:08:50.333 --> 00:08:51.625
No. No.

115
00:08:52.666 --> 00:08:54.958
Now, that's a yes!

116
00:08:55.041 --> 00:08:57.208
Cat!

117
00:08:58.875 --> 00:09:00.000
Oh, dear.

118
00:09:01.708 --> 00:09:03.791
Silly bird, fly!

119
00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:04.916
What? Wait!

120
00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.625
- Why aren't you flying?
- Oof!

121
00:09:14.708 --> 00:09:16.083
I can't fly.

122
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.416
Why aren't <i>you</i> flying?

123
00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.958
- Well, I've got a broken wing!
- Oh, no. How did that happen?

124
00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.958
Magpie? Wait for me!

125
00:09:35.125 --> 00:09:36.125
Phew!

126
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:39.791
- Let's get you safe indoors, hey?
- Thanks. Is the cat still...

127
00:09:40.416 --> 00:09:41.833
Poor little thing.

128
00:09:47.708 --> 00:09:48.875
Oh, awful!

129
00:09:48.958 --> 00:09:50.750
Out there all by yourself...

130
00:09:50.833 --> 00:09:53.333
Oh! Oh.

131
00:09:53.416 --> 00:09:55.250
Oh. Uh...

132
00:09:55.333 --> 00:09:58.791
- Are we safe in here?
- Ah. Yes. We're safe.

133
00:09:58.875 --> 00:10:01.750
The thorns keep unwanted visitors out.

134
00:10:02.583 --> 00:10:03.750
Usually.

135
00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:04.958
Oh, good.

136
00:10:05.708 --> 00:10:07.666
Is this your house?

137
00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.375
It's very...

138
00:10:11.416 --> 00:10:15.875
Oh. Why, thank you.
I suppose it is rather, um...

139
00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:17.416
Perfect.

140
00:10:18.041 --> 00:10:19.708
Well...

141
00:10:19.791 --> 00:10:20.625
Oh.

142
00:10:20.708 --> 00:10:22.875
A who-man house.

143
00:10:22.958 --> 00:10:25.791
Bet they've got loads
of crumbs in there.

144
00:10:25.875 --> 00:10:28.083
Oh. Them. Yes.

145
00:10:28.583 --> 00:10:30.791
They've got loads of everything.

146
00:10:32.291 --> 00:10:36.666
And all because of that
magic shiny wishing star, eh?

147
00:10:37.291 --> 00:10:38.416
Yeah.

148
00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.166
- The magic shiny...
- Mm.

149
00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.750
Wait. Sorry, what?

150
00:10:42.833 --> 00:10:43.833
The star.

151
00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:45.083
You don't...

152
00:10:46.166 --> 00:10:47.166
Right!

153
00:10:47.541 --> 00:10:49.583
Okay. It must be here somewhere.

154
00:10:51.666 --> 00:10:57.291
Once a year, the who-mans
take the spikiest tree in the woods,

155
00:10:57.375 --> 00:10:59.750
cover it in tin-soil and boo-bells,

156
00:10:59.833 --> 00:11:03.750
until their tree
is all twinkling and beautiful.

157
00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:05.250
Just like mine.

158
00:11:08.541 --> 00:11:13.708
Then, they put a shiny magic star on top,

159
00:11:13.791 --> 00:11:19.375
make a wish, and in the morning,
they get anything they want.

160
00:11:19.458 --> 00:11:20.375
Oh.

161
00:11:20.458 --> 00:11:21.291
Like crumbs.

162
00:11:21.375 --> 00:11:23.000
Crumbs?

163
00:11:23.083 --> 00:11:25.000
Don't be absurd.

164
00:11:25.083 --> 00:11:27.833
Well, what could be better than crumbs?

165
00:11:27.916 --> 00:11:30.291
"What could be better than..."

166
00:11:30.375 --> 00:11:32.500
Things!

167
00:11:36.583 --> 00:11:37.458
Huh?

168
00:11:37.541 --> 00:11:40.166
<i>♪ Things, they make you happy ♪</i>

169
00:11:40.666 --> 00:11:43.166
<i>♪ Things won't fly away ♪</i>

170
00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.125
<i>♪ Things will stick... ♪ </i>Ow.

171
00:11:45.208 --> 00:11:51.000
<i>♪ ...with you till the end
Oh, yes, on things you can depend ♪</i>

172
00:11:52.166 --> 00:11:55.208
<i>♪ See my bathtub? It's designer ♪</i>

173
00:11:55.291 --> 00:11:56.916
<i>♪ Finest china! Well, kinda ♪</i>

174
00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:00.916
<i>♪ Simply must have the latest bottle top
I love it so, I'll never stop ♪</i>

175
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.750
<i>♪ This chair? Hedgehog hair ♪</i>

176
00:12:02.833 --> 00:12:04.416
<i>♪ Pamperclips? I've got the pair ♪</i>

177
00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.250
<i>♪ This is a limited edition ♪</i>

178
00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:09.250
<i>♪ Piece of string ♪</i>

179
00:12:09.333 --> 00:12:13.625
<i>♪ I was a bird who couldn't fly
Felt tiny while they flew up high ♪</i>

180
00:12:14.625 --> 00:12:17.625
<i>♪ Surrounded myself
With things so gorgeous ♪</i>

181
00:12:17.708 --> 00:12:19.750
<i>♪ Felt enormous!</i> ♪

182
00:12:19.833 --> 00:12:21.500
<i>♪ So afraid and alone</i> ♪

183
00:12:21.583 --> 00:12:24.125
<i>♪ Things turn a hovel to a home</i> ♪

184
00:12:24.208 --> 00:12:27.500
<i>♪ Got no personality?
I let my lampshade speak for me ♪</i>

185
00:12:27.583 --> 00:12:31.916
<i>♪ Hollow inside? You're not enough?
Just stuff that hole with lovely stuff ♪</i>

186
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.083
<i>♪ Things are things that make you happy
Who needs friends? I've got a shoe chair ♪</i>

187
00:12:36.166 --> 00:12:40.708
<i>♪ No one there for you to care for?
Polish up your silverware for? ♪</i>

188
00:12:40.791 --> 00:12:47.791
<i>♪ There's no better company
Than one penny ♪</i>

189
00:12:56.333 --> 00:12:59.875
Look, my point is,
wish for something far better than crumbs.

190
00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.500
Oh. Right.

191
00:13:05.541 --> 00:13:07.416
Better than crumbs?

192
00:13:08.166 --> 00:13:09.000
Hm.

193
00:13:14.458 --> 00:13:17.250
Like a... Like a whole sandwich!

194
00:13:17.333 --> 00:13:18.750
Never mind.

195
00:13:19.416 --> 00:13:20.416
Okay, then.

196
00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:21.833
I'll do it.

197
00:13:21.875 --> 00:13:23.791
- Do what?
- I'll go get the star.

198
00:13:23.875 --> 00:13:27.416
Impossible! It's inside the who-man house.

199
00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.500
Tsk.

200
00:13:28.541 --> 00:13:31.625
Maybe I forgot to mention?
I was raised by mice.

201
00:13:31.708 --> 00:13:32.791
Explains the ears.

202
00:13:32.875 --> 00:13:35.500
And if there's one thing
us mice are good at,

203
00:13:35.583 --> 00:13:36.833
it's sneaking.

204
00:13:39.416 --> 00:13:40.250
Sorry, what?

205
00:13:40.333 --> 00:13:42.416
Oh, like, into houses.

206
00:13:43.458 --> 00:13:46.250
To get stuff. Like, stealing it.

207
00:13:46.333 --> 00:13:47.791
Right.

208
00:13:48.333 --> 00:13:52.916
Right!

209
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.000
Show me.

210
00:14:04.875 --> 00:14:06.000
What are you doing?

211
00:14:06.083 --> 00:14:08.916
- You're supposed to wait outside.
- I thought that we were...

212
00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.666
Who-mans!

213
00:14:27.833 --> 00:14:28.833
Okay.

214
00:14:29.833 --> 00:14:32.125
We're going to have to be
the sneakiest mice...

215
00:14:32.208 --> 00:14:34.000
...we've ever been.

216
00:14:34.083 --> 00:14:36.250
<i>- ♪ Ba-dum-bum-bum ♪</i>
- I'm not a mouse.

217
00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:37.750
Shh!

218
00:14:37.833 --> 00:14:40.041
Just do exactly what I do.

219
00:14:41.083 --> 00:14:43.375
<i>♪ Da-da-da-da-du-dum ♪</i>

220
00:14:43.458 --> 00:14:44.291
Ah!

221
00:14:44.375 --> 00:14:45.250
<i>♪ Da-da ♪</i>

222
00:14:45.333 --> 00:14:46.541
Da!

223
00:14:46.625 --> 00:14:47.708
<i>♪ Da-da-da ♪</i>

224
00:14:47.791 --> 00:14:49.000
Doh!

225
00:14:51.416 --> 00:14:52.875
<i>♪ Da-da-da ♪</i>

226
00:14:55.666 --> 00:14:57.208
<i>♪ Da-da-da-da ♪</i>

227
00:14:59.541 --> 00:15:00.541
<i>♪ Da-da ♪</i>

228
00:15:00.625 --> 00:15:03.625
<i>♪ Da-da-da-da-da ♪</i>

229
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.291
Hmm.

230
00:15:14.625 --> 00:15:16.083
<i>♪ Ba-ba-ba ♪</i>

231
00:15:16.166 --> 00:15:17.666
<i>♪ Ba-ba-ba-ba ♪</i>

232
00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.750
<i>♪ Ba-ba-ba-ba-ba ♪</i>

233
00:15:20.833 --> 00:15:23.750
<i>♪ Bi-dah-ba-dum-bum-bum ♪</i>

234
00:15:23.833 --> 00:15:26.541
<i>♪ Ba-dum-bum-bum
Ba-ba-doo-ba-da-da-da ♪</i>

235
00:15:26.625 --> 00:15:28.708
<i>♪ Ba-li-bi-di-la-ba-rum ♪</i>

236
00:15:28.791 --> 00:15:30.166
Shh!

237
00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.875
What are you doing?
You'll wake the who-mans!

238
00:15:32.958 --> 00:15:34.833
I'm... I'm being a sneaky mouse.

239
00:15:34.916 --> 00:15:36.375
That's not sneaking.

240
00:15:36.458 --> 00:15:40.625
The whole point of being a mouse
is you don't draw attention to yourself.

241
00:15:46.666 --> 00:15:47.708
Careful.

242
00:15:48.791 --> 00:15:52.458
Care... ful.

243
00:15:52.541 --> 00:15:54.583
Ow!

244
00:15:54.666 --> 00:15:56.291
Got it! Oh.

245
00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:00.833
Who-mans!

246
00:16:07.291 --> 00:16:10.750
Hah! Not bad for a couple
of flightless fools, eh?

247
00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.916
Why is it you don't fly?

248
00:16:14.416 --> 00:16:17.500
Oh. I just never learned.
I mean, mice don't fly!

249
00:16:21.333 --> 00:16:23.291
Well, it's easy! You just flap!

250
00:16:23.375 --> 00:16:25.625
No, thanks. I'll just...

251
00:16:28.125 --> 00:16:29.208
All right!

252
00:16:33.625 --> 00:16:35.333
Oh, you're a natural!

253
00:16:35.416 --> 00:16:36.500
Ahh!

254
00:16:39.375 --> 00:16:41.666
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

255
00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.083
Whoa!

256
00:16:45.708 --> 00:16:47.958
- Whoa!
- Woo-hoo!

257
00:16:53.375 --> 00:16:54.875
Oh!

258
00:16:58.708 --> 00:16:59.708
Oh, dear.

259
00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.458
The star!

260
00:17:18.666 --> 00:17:19.833
Per...

261
00:17:21.166 --> 00:17:22.541
...fect.

262
00:17:26.666 --> 00:17:27.666
Hm.

263
00:17:31.166 --> 00:17:32.958
- Hello.
- Ahh!

264
00:17:35.541 --> 00:17:37.125
What's this?

265
00:17:37.916 --> 00:17:40.333
An unexpected visitor.

266
00:17:40.416 --> 00:17:42.208
Hm.

267
00:17:42.291 --> 00:17:43.125
Why...

268
00:17:44.708 --> 00:17:46.916
...it's the little bird who

269
00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.583
sneaks about on the floor like a...

270
00:17:50.708 --> 00:17:51.916
mouse?

271
00:17:54.291 --> 00:17:59.583
And who are you trying to fool
with those... funny things?

272
00:18:02.458 --> 00:18:05.666
- My family are mice, so...
- Mice? Oh.

273
00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.500
Oh, and the ears are...

274
00:18:07.583 --> 00:18:09.333
Oh.

275
00:18:09.416 --> 00:18:11.583
Oh, I see.

276
00:18:11.666 --> 00:18:15.250
So tragic. So sad.

277
00:18:15.333 --> 00:18:17.750
Trying to <i>fit in.</i>

278
00:18:19.083 --> 00:18:21.333
You know you'll never be a real mouse.

279
00:18:22.166 --> 00:18:23.166
Oh, no, I...

280
00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.416
You see,

281
00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.916
you're a misfit.

282
00:18:27.583 --> 00:18:28.750
You're an oddball.

283
00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.625
You're a freak.

284
00:18:30.708 --> 00:18:32.000
No, I'm not.

285
00:18:32.083 --> 00:18:34.541
<i>♪ Micey ears atop a birdy beak ♪</i>

286
00:18:34.625 --> 00:18:35.541
Well, yeah.

287
00:18:35.625 --> 00:18:39.916
<i>♪ But I've never seen a bird
So peculiar, so absurd ♪</i>

288
00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:44.416
<i>♪ How about we play a game
Of hide-and-seek, if you can? ♪</i>

289
00:18:45.208 --> 00:18:48.416
<i>♪ As a mouse, to me
You seem to be just terrible ♪</i>

290
00:18:49.041 --> 00:18:52.875
<i>♪ Fitting in is more
Than dress-up and pretend ♪</i>

291
00:18:52.958 --> 00:18:57.125
<i>♪ If it's fitting in you're desperate for
Come down, search no more ♪</i>

292
00:18:57.208 --> 00:19:00.541
<i>♪ I know the perfect place
For you, my friend ♪</i>

293
00:19:00.625 --> 00:19:03.541
<i>♪ For you, I've the perfect place ♪</i>

294
00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:07.416
<i>♪ Not picky, stick with me
What's in a name? ♪</i>

295
00:19:07.916 --> 00:19:11.666
<i>♪ A robin or a mouse? ♪</i>

296
00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:15.750
<i>♪ After all, under the skin
You're all the same ♪</i>

297
00:19:15.833 --> 00:19:19.291
<i>♪ It's what's inside that counts ♪</i>

298
00:19:19.375 --> 00:19:22.333
<i>♪ Fitting in could be a breeze ♪</i>

299
00:19:23.333 --> 00:19:26.166
<i>♪ Just a squash and a squeeze</i> ♪

300
00:19:27.458 --> 00:19:30.583
<i>♪ Brush out those ears
Come along with me ♪</i>

301
00:19:31.583 --> 00:19:35.125
<i>♪ Quick as a glug
You could be sitting snug, perfectly ♪</i>

302
00:19:35.208 --> 00:19:38.416
<i>♪ You don't fit in
But you'd fit into my belly ♪</i>

303
00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:42.291
<i>♪ For you, I've the perfect place ♪</i>

304
00:19:42.375 --> 00:19:45.500
<i>♪ For you, I've the perfect place ♪</i>

305
00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:50.583
You really are a terrible mouse

306
00:19:50.666 --> 00:19:54.541
with nowhere left to sneak.

307
00:19:56.875 --> 00:19:58.625
Robin! And the star!

308
00:19:58.708 --> 00:20:00.291
And the...

309
00:20:00.375 --> 00:20:01.208
This is bad.

310
00:20:01.291 --> 00:20:02.791
Ge-ge... Get back!

311
00:20:03.875 --> 00:20:04.708
Oops.

312
00:20:04.791 --> 00:20:06.833
Oh. That's made it worse.

313
00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:09.750
Ahh!

314
00:20:15.791 --> 00:20:16.791
Oh!

315
00:20:23.041 --> 00:20:26.083
We did it! Everlasting happiness awaits!

316
00:20:26.166 --> 00:20:28.833
Told you us mice are good at... sneaking.

317
00:20:28.916 --> 00:20:31.458
Sneaking?

318
00:20:33.125 --> 00:20:36.166
You know,
I think we make very bad mice.

319
00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.208
Yes. Quite terrible.

320
00:20:39.208 --> 00:20:42.875
- But who cares? We got the star!
- Terrible?

321
00:20:44.083 --> 00:20:46.791
I'm not a terrible mouse.

322
00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:49.875
Am I?

323
00:20:58.541 --> 00:21:00.541
Ah!

324
00:21:03.833 --> 00:21:04.750
This goes here.

325
00:21:04.833 --> 00:21:05.833
Oh, oh, oh!

326
00:21:05.916 --> 00:21:06.750
There we go.

327
00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.541
Isn't this wonderful?

328
00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.041
Suppose so.

329
00:21:14.625 --> 00:21:18.041
Well, I hope you thought
of something better to wish for

330
00:21:18.125 --> 00:21:19.666
than a soggy old sandwich.

331
00:21:20.625 --> 00:21:24.708
You know, like a hubcap.
Or a shiny fork. Or a pencil sharpener.

332
00:21:24.791 --> 00:21:26.875
Or... a thimble.

333
00:21:26.958 --> 00:21:30.000
Or how about a safety pin...

334
00:21:33.416 --> 00:21:36.500
Hmm. Yeah.

335
00:21:43.708 --> 00:21:44.708
Oh!

336
00:21:45.833 --> 00:21:49.375
Well, I... I wish I wasn't a bird.

337
00:21:51.041 --> 00:21:53.333
I wish I was a mouse.

338
00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:55.541
A real one.

339
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:13.916
Magpie?

340
00:22:19.125 --> 00:22:21.375
Robin?

341
00:22:23.333 --> 00:22:24.166
It...

342
00:22:24.250 --> 00:22:26.416
It didn't work.

343
00:22:27.041 --> 00:22:28.041
Did it?

344
00:22:29.125 --> 00:22:30.125
No.

345
00:22:36.791 --> 00:22:38.458
Come now.

346
00:22:38.541 --> 00:22:40.875
It was always a bit of a long shot, eh?

347
00:22:40.958 --> 00:22:42.791
Stars and wishes. Hmm.

348
00:22:42.875 --> 00:22:44.208
A fool's dream...

349
00:22:44.291 --> 00:22:47.000
...was what it was.

350
00:22:48.458 --> 00:22:49.291
A mad...

351
00:22:52.833 --> 00:22:54.000
...fool's...

352
00:22:57.375 --> 00:22:58.708
...dream!

353
00:23:03.083 --> 00:23:04.791
It... It... It works!

354
00:23:04.875 --> 00:23:07.291
- Huh?
- Robin! The star!

355
00:23:07.875 --> 00:23:08.875
It works!

356
00:23:08.958 --> 00:23:10.583
Woo-hoo-hoo!

357
00:23:15.791 --> 00:23:16.916
A real one.

358
00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:19.375
What's that? For me?

359
00:23:19.458 --> 00:23:20.833
A lovely, shiny...

360
00:23:22.083 --> 00:23:23.916
Wonderful!

361
00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.458
What the...

362
00:23:28.625 --> 00:23:30.125
- Robin!
- Robin!

363
00:23:30.791 --> 00:23:31.875
- Robin!
- Huh?

364
00:23:32.583 --> 00:23:34.708
Uh... Dad?

365
00:23:34.791 --> 00:23:37.625
Oh! We've been looking everywhere for you!

366
00:23:38.125 --> 00:23:39.958
- Robin?
- Sorry, I...

367
00:23:40.541 --> 00:23:43.250
I went to sneak us some crumbs, but,

368
00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:45.333
it all went wrong.

369
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:48.375
Because, well,

370
00:23:49.333 --> 00:23:50.333
I think I'm a

371
00:23:51.416 --> 00:23:52.541
terrible mouse.

372
00:23:56.416 --> 00:23:57.458
Robin...

373
00:23:57.541 --> 00:24:00.250
I couldn't have said it better myself.

374
00:24:01.833 --> 00:24:04.083
Oh! In! In!

375
00:24:05.666 --> 00:24:06.750
A kitten!

376
00:24:13.208 --> 00:24:15.333
It's all right.

377
00:24:18.916 --> 00:24:21.458
Don't worry.
There's no way she could fit through the...

378
00:24:22.458 --> 00:24:23.291
...door!

379
00:24:25.916 --> 00:24:27.208
Oh, look.

380
00:24:27.291 --> 00:24:30.541
It's the whole family.

381
00:24:32.833 --> 00:24:33.666
Oh...

382
00:24:37.791 --> 00:24:39.291
What are you doing?

383
00:24:45.791 --> 00:24:49.958
Huh?

384
00:24:50.541 --> 00:24:52.541
- Robin!
- What <i>is</i> she doing?

385
00:24:53.166 --> 00:24:55.666
She's being a terrible mouse.

386
00:24:59.875 --> 00:25:02.500
Oh! Ooh! Ugh!

387
00:25:04.541 --> 00:25:07.333
<i>♪ The rules of The Sneak are these ♪</i>

388
00:25:07.416 --> 00:25:09.666
And that! And this! And that!

389
00:25:11.791 --> 00:25:12.625
Hah!

390
00:25:31.458 --> 00:25:33.000
You

391
00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.541
really

392
00:25:35.625 --> 00:25:38.666
are a terrible,

393
00:25:38.750 --> 00:25:42.208
terrible, terrible

394
00:25:42.916 --> 00:25:44.416
mouse...

395
00:25:46.875 --> 00:25:52.250
...with nowhere left to sneak.

396
00:25:53.166 --> 00:25:54.166
Wait.

397
00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:56.625
I don't... I don't need to sneak.

398
00:25:57.916 --> 00:25:59.666
I'm a... I'm a bir...

399
00:26:02.458 --> 00:26:03.291
...d.

400
00:26:07.083 --> 00:26:08.083
Robin!

401
00:26:12.125 --> 00:26:13.625
Robin!

402
00:26:13.708 --> 00:26:15.250
<i>♪ Da-da-da-da ♪</i>

403
00:26:34.250 --> 00:26:36.083
Woo-hoo!

404
00:26:36.833 --> 00:26:38.875
- Oof!
- Ooh. Ouch.

405
00:26:40.666 --> 00:26:41.666
Oof!

406
00:26:42.666 --> 00:26:44.750
- Robin!
- Dad!

407
00:26:46.166 --> 00:26:47.000
Robin!

408
00:26:47.083 --> 00:26:48.958
That was the most un-sneaky...

409
00:26:49.041 --> 00:26:50.875
- And stupid...
- And brilliant...

410
00:26:50.958 --> 00:26:53.541
Birdy-mousy thing we've ever seen!

411
00:26:53.625 --> 00:26:56.583
Robin, you were marvelous.

412
00:26:57.208 --> 00:26:58.041
Oh.

413
00:26:58.125 --> 00:26:59.708
Thanks, Dad.

414
00:26:59.791 --> 00:27:03.125
Robin, you're... you're not a mouse.

415
00:27:04.083 --> 00:27:05.541
But of course,

416
00:27:06.041 --> 00:27:07.208
you're a mouse.

417
00:27:07.791 --> 00:27:08.625
Huh?

418
00:27:08.708 --> 00:27:11.541
- Sorry, is that confusing?
- Yeah, what? She's a bird.

419
00:27:11.625 --> 00:27:14.875
Exactly. She is a bird,
and that's wonderful.

420
00:27:14.958 --> 00:27:19.833
And what I mean is,
we're the Mouse family.

421
00:27:19.916 --> 00:27:21.291
All of us.

422
00:27:22.583 --> 00:27:26.166
- Is the cat one of the family?
- No, Dink. The cat tried to eat us.

423
00:27:26.250 --> 00:27:27.708
Because she loves us?

424
00:27:27.791 --> 00:27:30.250
No. Because she's a predator.

425
00:27:30.333 --> 00:27:31.875
So, you fly now?

426
00:27:31.958 --> 00:27:33.958
Well, yeah. I guess so.

427
00:27:34.041 --> 00:27:37.833
But we're all still hungry,
and you've ruined Magpie's house.

428
00:27:37.916 --> 00:27:40.916
That's okay. They're only things.

429
00:27:43.125 --> 00:27:45.666
Yeah, and I'm bad at sneaking.

430
00:27:46.416 --> 00:27:49.041
If anything,
I just draw attention to myself.

431
00:28:00.416 --> 00:28:01.708
Mm.

432
00:28:08.625 --> 00:28:12.875
<i>♪ Hey! Over here!
A song for your ear ♪</i>

433
00:28:16.458 --> 00:28:18.625
<i>♪ While we keep to the shadows ♪</i>

434
00:28:18.708 --> 00:28:21.750
<i>♪ Don't get heard
Whisper every single word ♪</i>

435
00:28:21.833 --> 00:28:24.916
<i>♪ Ba-ba-bum-bum-bum-bum ♪</i>

436
00:28:25.916 --> 00:28:29.708
<i>♪ Look at me fly
Catching your eye ♪</i>

437
00:28:31.708 --> 00:28:33.875
<i>♪ With crumbs in our arms
And a raisin or two ♪</i>

438
00:28:33.958 --> 00:28:37.333
<i>♪ And a coin from the middle
Of this sticky brown poo ♪</i>

439
00:28:37.416 --> 00:28:41.583
<i>♪ Look at me
And you won't see my sneaky family ♪</i>

440
00:28:41.666 --> 00:28:43.750
<i>- ♪ Don't make a sound ♪
- ♪ Do make a sound ♪</i>

441
00:28:43.833 --> 00:28:46.208
<i>- ♪ Don't leave a trace ♪
- ♪ Do leave a trace ♪</i>

442
00:28:46.291 --> 00:28:48.208
<i>- ♪ Keep to the shadows ♪
- ♪ And the light ♪</i>

443
00:28:48.291 --> 00:28:50.333
<i>- ♪ What we need ♪</i>
- This is more than we need.

444
00:28:50.416 --> 00:28:51.625
- Magpie!
- Thank you!

445
00:28:51.708 --> 00:28:58.666
<i>♪ The rules of The Sneak are these</i> ♪

446
00:29:00.416 --> 00:29:01.250
Sorry!

447
00:29:02.750 --> 00:29:06.541
<i>♪ Dum-dum-dum ♪</i>

448
00:29:09.458 --> 00:29:10.916
- Wow!
- Well.

449
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:12.500
Hmm.

450
00:29:15.875 --> 00:29:17.416
It's a sandwich!
